{"type":"plan","title":"The Mended Kite","logline":"A gust tears a child's kite; a grandfather's sailor stitch and a gold star teach the wind to listen.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Morning wind whips the shingle beach; Maya stands on the pier flying her red kite high above the railings, the sea glittering under a pale sky.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"On a windy autumn morning in Brighton, eight-year-old Maya flies her red kite above the pier.","cites":[1,3,4,6]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"A sudden gust slams the kite into the iron railings; the red sail tears cleanly from corner to corner, string snapping taut.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"A gust slams it into the pier railings, and the red sail tears from corner to corner.","cites":[1,3,6]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Maya runs along the shingle beach toward home, the broken kite hugged tightly to her chest, wind tugging her hair.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs home along the seafront, the broken kite hugged to her chest.","cites":[1,3,4]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Over-the-shoulder","description":"Inside the sunlit kitchen, Grandfather looks up from his newspaper as Maya enters, the wooden table and window framing them.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Her grandfather, who mended sails when he was young, looks up from his newspaper.","cites":[2,3,4]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Insert/detail","description":"At the table Grandfather lays the kite flat, threads a needle with sailcloth thread, the newspaper folded beside him.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"At the kitchen table he lays the kite flat and threads a needle with sailcloth thread.","cites":[2,3,4]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Stitch by stitch Grandfather shows Maya the sailor's seam, his needle pulling the thread through the torn sail.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Stitch by stitch, he shows Maya how a sailor's seam holds against the wind.","cites":[2,3]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Maya dabs a tiny brush in gold paint and adds a five‑point star over the patch, the kite remembering the repair.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya paints a small gold star over the patch, so the kite will remember.","cites":[2,3,4]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Afternoon light bathes the pier; Maya and Grandfather walk side by side along the sand, the mended kite tucked under Grandfather's arm.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"In the afternoon they walk back to the beach together, the kite under Grandfather's arm.","cites":[1,3,4]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Maya sprints into the wind, the kite catching the gust and climbing higher than ever above the rolling waves.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs into the wind, and the kite climbs higher than ever over the waves.","cites":[1,3,6]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Maya hands the string to Grandfather; he throws his head back and laughs like a boy, the kite dancing overhead.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"She hands the string to her grandfather, and he laughs like a boy.","cites":[1,3,4]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Slow zoom-in","description":"Golden dusk paints the sand amber; Maya and Grandfather stroll home along the shore, the mended kite resting on Maya's shoulder, the pier fading behind them.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"At golden dusk they walk home along the sand, the mended kite on Maya's shoulder.","cites":[5,1,3,4]}]}
